module

public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.HighestWeight.Basic
import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.Submodule.Atom

public section

/-!
# Highest weight modules: the weight cone and the highest weight line

A **highest weight module** of weight `lam` is a module generated by a highest weight vector `v` of
weight `lam`, that is one with `LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤`. This file proves the two
structural facts that make the notion useful, both for an arbitrary such module, finite-dimensional
or not.

* Its weights lie in `lam - Q⁺`, where `Q⁺` is the cone of nonnegative integer combinations of the
  simple roots (`TauCeti.posRootCone`): the weight spaces at those weights already exhaust the
  module, so no other weight can occur.
* Its `lam`-weight space is the line `K ∙ v`, so `lam` really is the highest weight and `v` really
  is its highest weight vector, up to a nonzero scalar.

## The argument

Neither statement follows from the weight-space decomposition alone: the span of the weight spaces
at the weights `lam - ν` with `ν ∈ Q⁺` is *not* stable under `L`, a positive root vector moving the
top weight space out of the cone. What is true is that the module is already exhausted by the
negative nilradical `n⁻` acting on `v`, which is the statement `M = U(n⁻) · v` written before the
enveloping algebra is available: the `n⁻`-submodule `LieSubmodule.lieSpan K n⁻ {v}` generated by
`v` is the whole of `M`.

The key point is that this `n⁻`-submodule is stable under the Borel subalgebra `𝔟 = H + n⁺`, by
induction over the elements of a Lie span: moving `x ∈ 𝔟` past a bracket with `f ∈ n⁻` costs a term
`⁅⁅x, f⁆, -⁆`, and the triangular decomposition `L = n⁻ + 𝔟`
(`TauCeti.negativeNilradical_sup_borelSubalgebra_eq_top`) splits `⁅x, f⁆` into a piece that stays
inside the span and a piece the inductive hypothesis handles. With `𝔟` and `n⁻` both preserving it,
the `n⁻`-span is an `L`-submodule containing `v`, hence everything. That is
`TauCeti.lieSpan_toSubmodule_le_of_isHighestWeightVector`, and every result below is read off it by
exhibiting one `n⁻`-stable submodule.

The rest is bookkeeping against the cone. The span of the weight spaces at the weights `lam - ν`
with `ν ∈ Q⁺` is such a submodule, so it is everything, and the independence of the weight spaces
(`LieModule.iSupIndep_genWeightSpace`) converts that into a statement about individual weights.
Taking the indexing set to exclude `lam` itself is what isolates the highest weight line, and it is
legitimate because a positive root is never cancelled inside the cone
(`TauCeti.root_add_ne_zero_of_mem_posRoots_of_mem_posRootCone`).

## Main results

* `TauCeti.lieSpan_toSubmodule_le_of_isHighestWeightVector` and
  `TauCeti.eq_top_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top`: a submodule containing a highest
  weight vector and stable under the negative nilradical already contains everything that vector
  generates under all of `L`, so in a highest weight module it is the whole module.
* `TauCeti.iSup_genWeightSpace_sub_posRootCone_eq_top_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top`:
  the weight spaces at the weights `lam - ν`, `ν ∈ Q⁺`, span a highest weight module.
* `TauCeti.exists_sub_eq_of_genWeightSpace_ne_bot_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top`: hence
  every weight of a highest weight module is of the form `lam - ν` with `ν ∈ Q⁺`;
  `TauCeti.sub_mem_posRootCone_of_genWeightSpace_ne_bot_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top`
  restates that for a weight given as a linear form, and
  `TauCeti.eq_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top` deduces that a module is a highest weight
  module for at most one weight;
  `TauCeti.IsHighestWeightVector.unique_of_isIrreducible` specializes this to irreducible modules.
* `TauCeti.genWeightSpace_eq_span_singleton_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top`: the
  `lam`-weight space of a highest weight module is the line spanned by its highest weight vector.
* `TauCeti.exists_eq_smul_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top`: consequently any highest
  weight vector of weight `lam` in it is a nonzero multiple of the generating one.

## References

This file supplies the "highest weight modules" half of the "highest weight vectors and modules"
item of Layer 3 of `TauCetiRoadmap/RepresentationTheory/LieHighestWeight/README.md`: "a highest
weight module of weight `λ` is one generated by such a `v`; its weights all lie in `λ - (ℕ-span of
simple roots)`, and its `λ`-weight space is the line `K·v`".

* J. E. Humphreys, *Introduction to Lie Algebras and Representation Theory*, GTM 9, §20.2.
-/

namespace TauCeti

open LieAlgebra LieModule Module

universe u v w

variable {K : Type u} {L : Type v} [Field K] [CharZero K] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]
  [IsKilling K L] [FiniteDimensional K L]
  {H : LieSubalgebra K L} [H.IsCartanSubalgebra] [IsTriangularizable K H L]
  {M : Type w} [AddCommGroup M] [Module K M] [LieRingModule L M] [LieModule K L M]

/-! ### The triangular decomposition of a stability condition -/

variable (H)
variable (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base)

/-- **The triangular decomposition, as a splitting of an element of `L`**: every `x : L` is the sum
of an element of the negative nilradical and an element of the Borel subalgebra. -/
private theorem exists_mem_negativeNilradical_add_mem_borelSubalgebra (x : L) :
    ∃ g ∈ negativeNilradical H b, ∃ y ∈ borelSubalgebra H b, g + y = x := by
  refine Submodule.mem_sup.mp ?_
  rw [negativeNilradical_sup_borelSubalgebra_eq_top]
  trivial

omit [LieModule K L M] in
/-- **A submodule stable under `n⁻` and under `𝔟` is stable under `L`**, by the triangular
decomposition `L = n⁻ + (H + n⁺)`. -/
private theorem lie_mem_of_lie_mem_negativeNilradical_of_lie_mem_borelSubalgebra
    (N : Submodule K M) (hneg : ∀ x ∈ negativeNilradical H b, ∀ m ∈ N, ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ N)
    (hbor : ∀ x ∈ borelSubalgebra H b, ∀ m ∈ N, ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ N) {x : L} {m : M} (hm : m ∈ N) :
    ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ N := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg, y, hy, rfl⟩ := exists_mem_negativeNilradical_add_mem_borelSubalgebra H b x
  rw [add_lie]
  exact add_mem (hneg g hg m hm) (hbor y hy m hm)

variable {H b}
variable {lam : Dual K H} {v : M}

/-! ### The submodule generated by the lowering operators -/

/-- **The `n⁻`-submodule generated by a highest weight vector is stable under the Borel
subalgebra.** For `x ∈ 𝔟` and a member `⁅f, m⁆` of the span with `f ∈ n⁻`, the Leibniz rule
replaces `⁅x, ⁅f, m⁆⁆` by `⁅⁅x, f⁆, m⁆ + ⁅f, ⁅x, m⁆⁆`; the second term stays inside the span by the
inductive hypothesis, and the first is handled by splitting `⁅x, f⁆` along the triangular
decomposition `L = n⁻ + 𝔟`. -/
private theorem lie_mem_lieSpan_of_mem_borelSubalgebra (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v) {m : M}
    (hm : m ∈ LieSubmodule.lieSpan K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) {v}) :
    ∀ x ∈ borelSubalgebra H b,
      ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ LieSubmodule.lieSpan K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) {v} := by
  induction hm using LieSubmodule.lieSpan_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hy
    subst hy
    intro x hx
    rw [← LieSubalgebra.mem_toSubmodule, borelSubalgebra_toSubmodule, Submodule.mem_sup] at hx
    obtain ⟨u, hu, p, hp, rfl⟩ := hx
    rw [add_lie, hv.lie_eq_smul ⟨u, hu⟩, hv.lie_eq_zero_of_mem_positiveNilradical hp, add_zero]
    exact SMulMemClass.smul_mem _ (LieSubmodule.subset_lieSpan rfl)
  | zero => intro x _; rw [lie_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add y z _ _ ihy ihz => intro x hx; rw [lie_add]; exact add_mem (ihy x hx) (ihz x hx)
  | smul c y _ ih => intro x hx; rw [lie_smul]; exact SMulMemClass.smul_mem _ (ih x hx)
  | lie f y hy ih =>
    intro x hx
    rw [LieSubalgebra.coe_bracket_of_module, leibniz_lie]
    refine add_mem ?_ (LieSubmodule.lie_mem _ (x := f) (ih x hx))
    obtain ⟨g, hg, z, hz, hgz⟩ :=
      exists_mem_negativeNilradical_add_mem_borelSubalgebra H b ⁅x, (f : L)⁆
    rw [← hgz, add_lie]
    exact add_mem
      (LieSubmodule.lie_mem _ (x := (⟨g, hg⟩ : ↥(negativeNilradical H b))) hy) (ih z hz)

/-- Everything a highest weight vector generates under `L` it already generates under `n⁻`: the
`n⁻`-span is stable under `n⁻` by construction and under `𝔟` by
`TauCeti.lie_mem_lieSpan_of_mem_borelSubalgebra`, hence under all of `L`. -/
private theorem lieSpan_toSubmodule_le_lieSpan_negativeNilradical
    (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v) :
    (LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} : Submodule K M)
      ≤ (LieSubmodule.lieSpan K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) {v} : Submodule K M) := by
  have hneg : ∀ x ∈ negativeNilradical H b,
      ∀ m ∈ (LieSubmodule.lieSpan K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) {v} : Submodule K M),
        ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ (LieSubmodule.lieSpan K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) {v} : Submodule K M) :=
    fun x hx _ hm => LieSubmodule.lie_mem _ (x := (⟨x, hx⟩ : ↥(negativeNilradical H b))) hm
  have hbor : ∀ x ∈ borelSubalgebra H b,
      ∀ m ∈ (LieSubmodule.lieSpan K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) {v} : Submodule K M),
        ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ (LieSubmodule.lieSpan K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) {v} : Submodule K M) :=
    fun x hx _ hm => lie_mem_lieSpan_of_mem_borelSubalgebra hv hm x hx
  have hv0 : v ∈ (LieSubmodule.lieSpan K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) {v} : Submodule K M) :=
    LieSubmodule.subset_lieSpan rfl
  refine fun m hm => (LieSubmodule.lieSpan_le (N := ({
      __ := (LieSubmodule.lieSpan K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) {v} : Submodule K M),
      lie_mem := fun hm =>
        lie_mem_of_lie_mem_negativeNilradical_of_lie_mem_borelSubalgebra H b _ hneg hbor hm } :
          LieSubmodule K L M))).mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hv0) hm

/-- **A submodule containing a highest weight vector and stable under the negative nilradical
contains everything that vector generates under all of `L`.** This is the content of
`M = U(n⁻) · v`, written before the enveloping algebra is available: no hypothesis on the module is
needed, only that `v` is a highest weight vector. -/
theorem lieSpan_toSubmodule_le_of_isHighestWeightVector (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v)
    {N : Submodule K M} (hvN : v ∈ N)
    (hstab : ∀ x ∈ negativeNilradical H b, ∀ m ∈ N, ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ N) :
    (LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} : Submodule K M) ≤ N := by
  refine (lieSpan_toSubmodule_le_lieSpan_negativeNilradical hv).trans fun m hm => ?_
  exact (LieSubmodule.lieSpan_le (N := ({ __ := N, lie_mem := fun {x _} hm => hstab x x.2 _ hm } :
    LieSubmodule K ↥(negativeNilradical H b) M))).mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hvN) hm

/-- **A highest weight module is exhausted by the negative nilradical acting on its generator.** A
submodule containing the generator and stable under `n⁻` is the whole module. -/
theorem eq_top_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v)
    (hgen : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤) {N : Submodule K M} (hvN : v ∈ N)
    (hstab : ∀ x ∈ negativeNilradical H b, ∀ m ∈ N, ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ N) : N = ⊤ :=
  eq_top_iff.mpr fun m _ =>
    lieSpan_toSubmodule_le_of_isHighestWeightVector hv hvN hstab (by simp [hgen])

/-! ### The weights below the highest weight -/

/-- **The negative nilradical moves the span of a set `S` of weight spaces into the span of any set
`T` containing all shifts of `S` by negative roots.** Decomposing an element of `n⁻` into root
vectors reduces this to `TauCeti.lie_mem_genWeightSpaceSpan`. -/
private theorem lie_mem_genWeightSpaceSpan_of_mem_negativeNilradical {S T : Set (H → K)}
    (hST : ∀ gamma ∈ negRoots (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b, ∀ chi ∈ S, (gamma : H → K) + chi ∈ T)
    {x : L} (hx : x ∈ negativeNilradical H b) {m : M} (hm : m ∈ genWeightSpaceSpan H M S) :
    ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ genWeightSpaceSpan H M T := by
  rw [mem_negativeNilradical, rootSpaceSpan_eq_iSup] at hx
  exact LieSubmodule.iSup_induction _ (motive := fun x => ⁅x, m⁆ ∈ genWeightSpaceSpan H M T) hx
    (fun gamma _ hy => lie_mem_genWeightSpaceSpan hy (hST gamma gamma.2) hm)
    (by simp) (fun y z hy hz => by rw [add_lie]; exact add_mem hy hz)

variable (b) in
/-- The weights of the form `lam - ν` with `ν` in the positive root cone. -/
private def lowerSet (lam : Dual K H) : Set (H → K) :=
  {chi | ∃ nu ∈ posRootCone (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b, ((lam - nu : Dual K H) : H → K) = chi}

variable (b) in
/-- The same weights with the top weight `lam` itself removed. -/
private def strictLowerSet (lam : Dual K H) : Set (H → K) :=
  {chi ∈ lowerSet b lam | chi ≠ ((lam : Dual K H) : H → K)}

private theorem self_mem_lowerSet : ((lam : Dual K H) : H → K) ∈ lowerSet b lam :=
  ⟨0, zero_mem _, by rw [sub_zero]⟩

/-- Negating a negative root gives a positive root, hence a member of the cone. -/
private theorem root_reflectionPerm_self_mem_posRootCone_of_mem_negRoots {gamma : H.root}
    (hgamma : gamma ∈ negRoots (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b) :
    (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root ((IsKilling.rootSystem H).reflectionPerm gamma gamma)
      ∈ posRootCone (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b :=
  root_mem_posRootCone_of_mem_posRoots (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b
    ((reflectionPerm_self_mem_posRoots_iff_mem_negRoots (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b gamma).mpr
      hgamma)

/-- Subtracting the negative of a root from `lam` is the same as adding the root, so a shift of the
cone member `nu` by `-root γ` shifts the weight `lam - nu` by `root γ`. -/
private theorem sub_root_reflectionPerm_self_add_eq_root_add_sub (gamma : H.root)
    (nu : Dual K H) :
    lam - ((IsKilling.rootSystem H).root
          ((IsKilling.rootSystem H).reflectionPerm gamma gamma) + nu)
      = (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root gamma + (lam - nu) := by
  rw [RootPairing.root_reflectionPerm, RootPairing.reflection_apply_self]
  abel

/-- The coercion of linear forms to functions turns the sum of a root and a weight into the
pointwise sum that indexes weight spaces. -/
private theorem coe_root_add (gamma : H.root) (chi : Dual K H) :
    (((IsKilling.rootSystem H).root gamma + chi : Dual K H) : H → K) = (gamma : H → K) + chi := by
  ext y
  simp

/-- Adding a negative root to a weight below `lam` keeps it below `lam`. -/
private theorem add_mem_lowerSet {gamma : H.root}
    (hgamma : gamma ∈ negRoots (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b) {chi : H → K}
    (hchi : chi ∈ lowerSet b lam) : (gamma : H → K) + chi ∈ lowerSet b lam := by
  obtain ⟨nu, hnu, rfl⟩ := hchi
  exact ⟨_, add_mem (root_reflectionPerm_self_mem_posRootCone_of_mem_negRoots hgamma) hnu, by
    rw [sub_root_reflectionPerm_self_add_eq_root_add_sub, coe_root_add]⟩

/-- Adding a negative root to a weight below `lam` moves it *strictly* below `lam`: a positive root
is never cancelled inside the cone. -/
private theorem add_mem_strictLowerSet {gamma : H.root}
    (hgamma : gamma ∈ negRoots (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b) {chi : H → K}
    (hchi : chi ∈ lowerSet b lam) : (gamma : H → K) + chi ∈ strictLowerSet b lam := by
  refine ⟨add_mem_lowerSet hgamma hchi, fun hcontra => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨nu, hnu, rfl⟩ := hchi
  rw [← coe_root_add] at hcontra
  have hdual : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root gamma + (lam - nu) = lam :=
    DFunLike.coe_injective hcontra
  have hroot : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root gamma = nu := by
    simpa using congrArg (· - (lam - nu)) hdual
  refine root_add_ne_zero_of_mem_posRoots_of_mem_posRootCone (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b
    ((reflectionPerm_self_mem_posRoots_iff_mem_negRoots (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b gamma).mpr
      hgamma) hnu ?_
  rw [RootPairing.root_reflectionPerm, RootPairing.reflection_apply_self, ← hroot]
  abel

/-! ### The weights of a highest weight module -/

/-- **The weight spaces below `lam` span a highest weight module.** Their span contains the
generator and is stable under the negative nilradical, because adding a negative root to a weight
below `lam` keeps it below `lam`. -/
theorem iSup_genWeightSpace_sub_posRootCone_eq_top_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top
    (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v) (hgen : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤) :
    ⨆ nu ∈ posRootCone (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b,
      genWeightSpace M ((lam - nu : Dual K H) : H → K) = ⊤ := by
  have hspan : (genWeightSpaceSpan H M (lowerSet b lam) : Submodule K M) = ⊤ :=
    eq_top_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top hv hgen
      (genWeightSpace_le_genWeightSpaceSpan self_mem_lowerSet hv.mem_genWeightSpace)
      fun _ hx _ hm => lie_mem_genWeightSpaceSpan_of_mem_negativeNilradical
        (fun _ hgamma _ hchi => add_mem_lowerSet hgamma hchi) hx hm
  have htop : genWeightSpaceSpan H M (lowerSet b lam) = ⊤ :=
    (LieSubmodule.toSubmodule_eq_top _).mp hspan
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr (htop ▸ genWeightSpaceSpan_le_iff.mpr fun chi hchi => ?_)
  obtain ⟨nu, hnu, rfl⟩ := hchi
  exact le_iSup₂_of_le nu hnu le_rfl

/-- **The weights of a highest weight module lie in `lam - Q⁺`.** A weight outside the cone would
have its weight space disjoint from the ones that already exhaust the module.

The weight is taken to be an arbitrary function `chi : H → K` rather than a linear form, because
`LieModule.Weight K H M` is only known to be linear when `M` is finite-dimensional; the conclusion
says in particular that every weight of a highest weight module *is* linear. -/
theorem exists_sub_eq_of_genWeightSpace_ne_bot_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top
    (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v) (hgen : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤) {chi : H → K}
    (hchi : genWeightSpace M chi ≠ ⊥) :
    ∃ nu ∈ posRootCone (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b, ((lam - nu : Dual K H) : H → K) = chi := by
  by_contra hcontra
  simp only [not_exists, not_and] at hcontra
  refine hchi (eq_bot_iff.mpr ?_)
  have hdisj := iSupIndep_genWeightSpace K H M chi
  have hle : (⊤ : LieSubmodule K H M) ≤ ⨆ psi, ⨆ (_ : psi ≠ chi), genWeightSpace M psi := by
    rw [← iSup_genWeightSpace_sub_posRootCone_eq_top_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top
      hv hgen]
    exact iSup₂_le fun nu hnu =>
      le_iSup₂_of_le ((lam - nu : Dual K H) : H → K) (hcontra nu hnu) le_rfl
  calc genWeightSpace M chi
      = genWeightSpace M chi ⊓ ⊤ := (inf_top_eq _).symm
    _ ≤ genWeightSpace M chi ⊓ ⨆ psi, ⨆ (_ : psi ≠ chi), genWeightSpace M psi :=
        inf_le_inf_left _ hle
    _ = ⊥ := disjoint_iff.mp hdisj

/-- **The weights of a highest weight module lie in `lam - Q⁺`**, for a weight presented as a
linear form on the Cartan subalgebra. -/
theorem sub_mem_posRootCone_of_genWeightSpace_ne_bot_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top
    (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v) (hgen : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤)
    {chi : Dual K H} (hchi : genWeightSpace M ((chi : Dual K H) : H → K) ≠ ⊥) :
    lam - chi ∈ posRootCone (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b := by
  obtain ⟨nu, hnu, heq⟩ :=
    exists_sub_eq_of_genWeightSpace_ne_bot_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top
      hv hgen hchi
  have hnu' : lam - nu = chi := DFunLike.coe_injective heq
  rwa [← hnu', sub_sub_cancel]

/-- **A module is a highest weight module for at most one weight.** If two highest weight vectors
both generate `M`, each of their weights lies below the other, and the cone is sharp. -/
theorem eq_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top {w : M} {mu : Dual K H}
    (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v) (hgv : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤)
    (hw : IsHighestWeightVector b mu w) (hgw : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {w} = ⊤) : lam = mu := by
  have hlam : lam - mu ∈ posRootCone (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b :=
    sub_mem_posRootCone_of_genWeightSpace_ne_bot_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top
      hv hgv hw.genWeightSpace_ne_bot
  have hmu : mu - lam ∈ posRootCone (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b :=
    sub_mem_posRootCone_of_genWeightSpace_ne_bot_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top
      hw hgw hv.genWeightSpace_ne_bot
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp
    (eq_zero_of_add_eq_zero_of_mem_posRootCone (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b hlam hmu (by abel))

/-- An irreducible module carries highest weight vectors of at most one weight. -/
theorem IsHighestWeightVector.unique_of_isIrreducible [LieModule.IsIrreducible K L M]
    {w : M} {mu : Dual K H} (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v)
    (hw : IsHighestWeightVector b mu w) : lam = mu :=
  eq_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top hv
    (lieSpan_singleton_eq_top_of_ne_zero hv.ne_zero) hw
    (lieSpan_singleton_eq_top_of_ne_zero hw.ne_zero)

/-! ### The highest weight line -/

/-- **The top weight space of a highest weight module is a line.** Splitting off the weight spaces
strictly below `lam`, what is left of the module at weight `lam` is the span of the generator. -/
theorem genWeightSpace_eq_span_singleton_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top
    (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v) (hgen : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤) :
    (genWeightSpace M ((lam : Dual K H) : H → K) : Submodule K M) = Submodule.span K {v} := by
  have hvmem : v ∈ (genWeightSpaceSpan H M (lowerSet b lam) : Submodule K M) :=
    genWeightSpace_le_genWeightSpaceSpan self_mem_lowerSet hv.mem_genWeightSpace
  -- the generator together with the weight spaces strictly below `lam` exhaust `M`
  have hsplit : Submodule.span K {v} ⊔
      (genWeightSpaceSpan H M (strictLowerSet b lam) : Submodule K M) = ⊤ := by
    refine eq_top_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top hv hgen
      (Submodule.mem_sup_left (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self v)) fun x hx m hm => ?_
    obtain ⟨y, hy, z, hz, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp hm
    rw [lie_add]
    refine add_mem ?_ (Submodule.mem_sup_right
      (lie_mem_genWeightSpaceSpan_of_mem_negativeNilradical
        (fun _ hgamma _ hchi => add_mem_strictLowerSet hgamma hchi.1) hx hz))
    obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mp hy
    rw [lie_smul]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.mem_sup_right
      (lie_mem_genWeightSpaceSpan_of_mem_negativeNilradical
        (fun _ hgamma _ hchi => add_mem_strictLowerSet hgamma hchi) hx hvmem))
  -- the `lam`-weight space meets those strictly lower weight spaces trivially
  have hdisj : Disjoint (genWeightSpace M ((lam : Dual K H) : H → K))
      (genWeightSpaceSpan H M (strictLowerSet b lam)) :=
    (iSupIndep_genWeightSpace K H M ((lam : Dual K H) : H → K)).mono_right
      (genWeightSpaceSpan_le_iff.mpr fun chi hchi => le_iSup₂_of_le chi hchi.2 le_rfl)
  have hdisj' : (genWeightSpace M ((lam : Dual K H) : H → K) : Submodule K M) ⊓
      (genWeightSpaceSpan H M (strictLowerSet b lam) : Submodule K M) = ⊥ := by
    rw [← LieSubmodule.inf_toSubmodule, disjoint_iff.mp hdisj, LieSubmodule.bot_toSubmodule]
  refine le_antisymm (fun m hm => ?_)
    (Submodule.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hv.mem_genWeightSpace))
  obtain ⟨y, hy, z, hz, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp (hsplit ▸ Submodule.mem_top (x := m))
  have hyw : y ∈ (genWeightSpace M ((lam : Dual K H) : H → K) : Submodule K M) :=
    Submodule.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hv.mem_genWeightSpace) hy
  have hzw : z ∈ (genWeightSpace M ((lam : Dual K H) : H → K) : Submodule K M) := by
    simpa only [add_sub_cancel_left] using sub_mem hm hyw
  have hz0 : z = 0 := by
    have : z ∈ (⊥ : Submodule K M) := hdisj' ▸ Submodule.mem_inf.mpr ⟨hzw, hz⟩
    simpa using this
  rw [hz0, add_zero]
  exact hy

/-- **A highest weight vector of weight `lam` in a highest weight module is a nonzero multiple of
the generator.** It lies in the `lam`-weight space, which is the line the generator spans. -/
theorem exists_eq_smul_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top {w : M}
    (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v) (hgen : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤)
    (hw : IsHighestWeightVector b lam w) : ∃ c : K, c ≠ 0 ∧ w = c • v := by
  have hmem : w ∈ Submodule.span K {v} := by
    rw [← genWeightSpace_eq_span_singleton_of_isHighestWeightVector_of_lieSpan_eq_top hv hgen]
    exact hw.mem_genWeightSpace
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mp hmem
  exact ⟨c, fun hzero => hw.ne_zero (by rw [← hc, hzero, zero_smul]), hc.symm⟩

end TauCeti
